# Simple smart answer

Ask only what people can reasonably know, and make every choice lead to a clear next step. A simple smart answer is a short question-and-outcome tree with no calculations. Shared decision-aid rules are on [Smart answer](../smart-answer.html), and shared limits are on [Page templates](../index.html).

## When to use it

Use it when someone needs to choose between a few guidance routes, such as installation instructions or colour-setting guidance. Ask only what they need to decide ([WG-054](../../../content/writing-guidelines/clear-structure.html#wg-054)). Each outcome should lead to a clear next step.

## Structure and behaviour

Keep questions short, choices easy to tell apart and an option for uncertainty. Keep the chosen answer visible while the person reads the result. A simple decision is often better as an ordinary list of links with explanatory text. Do not add a wizard only to imitate a template.

## Home Assistant boundary

The examples use direct links to real sections. They do not store answers or create a configuration. A more complex dependency graph needs a specified, tested implementation, not growing ad hoc conditional markup.

